        <ArticleTitle>Biomechanical analysis of clear aligner force systems in orthodontic tooth movement: a finite element study.</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE">To evaluate the biomechanical effects of clear aligners on orthodontic tooth movement using finite element analysis.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="METHODS">Three-dimensional finite element models were constructed from CBCT data of 10 patients. Force systems were simulated for various tooth movements including tipping, rotation, and bodily movement.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="RESULTS">Clear aligners produced predictable force systems for simple tipping movements but showed reduced efficiency for complex movements such as root torque and bodily translation.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
