        <ArticleTitle>Machine learning approaches for automated cephalometric landmark detection: a systematic review.</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>This systematic review evaluates the current state of machine learning methods for automated cephalometric landmark detection in orthodontic diagnosis. A comprehensive literature search identified 45 studies published between 2018 and 2024. Deep learning architectures, particularly convolutional neural networks, demonstrated accuracy comparable to expert clinicians for most landmarks.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
